MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: e9620f8c34305754d8cc9a7e49e852d9, type: 3}
  m_Name: Tutorial_en
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  m_LocaleId:
    m_Code: en
  m_SharedData: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 567da0f27ceb5364a9fea3c9364162c3, type: 2}
  m_Metadata:
    m_Items: []
  m_TableData:
  - m_Id: 773593087938560
    m_Localized: "In the employee screen, you can view the list of your workers,
      organized by department. Within each department, employees are arranged by
      their assigned team.\r\nNear the end of the list, you will find employees who
      have been hired but are not yet active, as they have not been assigned to any
      team.\r\nAt the bottom, you can search for new candidates to hire\u2014but
      keep in mind that each search comes at a cost!"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 773544673087488
    m_Localized: Employee List
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 773431074557952
    m_Localized: 'Time is a key resource in the game. You can pause the passing weeks
      by pressing the pause icon in the top panel, allowing you to manage employees
      and contracts at your own pace.

      Opening any other screen will automatically
      stop the game time.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 773376175312896
    m_Localized: Time Management
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 773202392715264
    m_Localized: Main Interface
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 773230901399552
    m_Localized: "From the main screen, you can review information about active departments,
      manage the company\u2019s employee list, and monitor ongoing contracts.\r\nIn
      the top-left corner, you will also find key company details: the number of
      employees, the time passed since the company\u2019s founding, and its current
      capital.\r\nTo become familiar with the interface, it is recommended to explore
      the screens in the following order: departments, employees, projects."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 772966798659584
    m_Localized: Goal of the Game
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 773064983121920
    m_Localized: The goal of the game is to grow the company while avoiding bankruptcy.
      To achieve this, it is essential to strengthen existing departments and unlock
      new ones, allowing you to offer clients increasingly advanced and innovative
      solutions while keeping pace with the market.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 772674849935360
    m_Localized: 'You will take on the role of the employer and manager of a growing
      IT company. Your task is to manage employees and departments to support its
      growth.

      As the game progresses, you will expand the company to offer
      new services to clients who will entrust you with the development of their
      projects.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 772635696107520
    m_Localized: Introduction to the Game
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 772448646926336
    m_Localized: "This video game is a thesis project dedicated to the development
      of a serious game designed to raise awareness of autism, with a particular
      focus on the potential of autistic individuals\u2014especially in the workplace,
      where their strengths and unique abilities can be fully recognized."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 772392208371712
    m_Localized: What is AUT-INC
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 772221651193856
    m_Localized: 'Welcome to AUT-INC!

      AUT-INC is a management game developed
      by Daniele Gentile, a student at the University of Bari Aldo Moro.

      Special
      thanks to Professor Veronica Rossano, Associate Professor at the Department
      of Computer Science, University of Bari Aldo Moro, for supervising the project
      and providing support during the development of AUT-INC.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 772112045641728
    m_Localized: AUT-INC
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 773976912891904
    m_Localized: Employee Information
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 774005882949632
    m_Localized: "By selecting an employee, you can view their details, analyze their
      profile, and change their team assignment.\r\nKeep in mind that removing an
      employee from a team will cause both them and their teammates to experience
      a temporary drop in morale, reducing overall productivity.\r\nIf you believe
      an employee is no longer contributing value to the company, you may dismiss
      them\u2014but doing so will require paying a severance fee."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 774180353413120
    m_Localized: Hiring New Employees
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 774315187703808
    m_Localized: 'In the candidate screen, you can review descriptions to assess
      their suitability for the position you intend to fill in your company. Multiple
      searches can be conducted consecutively, provided the associated cost is paid.

      Warning:
      requesting a new search will remove all current candidates from the list, replacing
      them with new ones. Make sure to review them carefully before proceeding.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 774477284970496
    m_Localized: 'In the project screen, you can view the list of projects currently
      being developed by the company. For each project, key information is provided:
      the remaining time until delivery and the work still required for completion.

      At
      the bottom of the list, a button allows access to projects that have been proposed
      to the company but not yet accepted.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 774446192594944
    m_Localized: Project List
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 774598252892160
    m_Localized: 'By selecting a project, you can view its details. You can see which
      departments are assigned to the project, how many weeks remain, and how much
      work is still required.

      Additionally, various financial details are
      available, including the advance payment, weekly payment, and final payment.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 774574848675840
    m_Localized: Project Information
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 774699759243264
    m_Localized: 'A project is considered complete if finished by the deadline, or
      incomplete if it does not allow delays.

      Upon completion, the final
      payment will be adjusted based on how many weeks early or late the project
      is delivered.

      If you fail to complete a project, you must pay a penalty
      for missing the deadline.

      If you are unsure about finishing a project,
      you may terminate the contract by paying a penalty, allowing your employees
      to focus on other projects.

'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 774697569816576
    m_Localized: Project Completion
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 775319954198528
    m_Localized: 'In the New Projects screen, you can view the requests submitted
      to your company. You can review project details to decide whether to accept
      or decline them.

      New projects change every week, so make sure to check
      regularly for interesting and profitable opportunities to pursue.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 775311402012672
    m_Localized: New Projects
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 775521297567744
    m_Localized: 'In each department screen, you can find a description of the tasks
      to be performed and the skills required to carry out the work effectively.

      Information
      is also provided on the number of employees, the monthly salary of each employee,
      the recommended number of teams, and the current number of teams in the department.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 775518277668864
    m_Localized: Departments
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 775817667088384
    m_Localized: "In this screen, you can view the department's team structure.\r\nTry
      to keep the number of teams as close as possible to the recommended value;
      otherwise, the department will be poorly organized and its productivity will
      decrease.\r\nAlso, pay attention to employees\u2019 preferences for working
      alone or in a group to keep them happy and boost their productivity."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 775793113632768
    m_Localized: Teams
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 775953231187968
    m_Localized: 'At any time, you can upgrade a department. Upgrading allows you
      to increase the maximum number of employees, boosting productivity.

      Keep
      in mind, however, that the recommended number of teams may change, and employee
      salaries will rise as the department becomes more specialized.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 775929000693760
    m_Localized: Department Upgrade
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  references:
    version: 2
    RefIds: []
